Here’s a set of 15 Linux command Q&A posts 👇

Q: How can you list all files, including hidden ones, in a directory?
A: ls -la

Q: How do you view the first 10 lines of a file?
A: head filename.txt

Q: What command displays the last 10 lines of a file in real-time?
A:  tail -f filename.log

Q: How can you check the current system uptime?
A: uptime

Q: How do you check disk space usage?
A: df -h

Q: How can you check memory usage in Linux?
A: free -h

Q: How do you find out which user you’re logged in as?
A:  whoami

Q: How do you search for a specific word inside files?
A: grep "keyword" filename.txt

Q: How can you view running processes on your system?
A: ps aux or top

Q: How can you see your system’s IP address?
A: ip addr show  or hostname -I

Q: How can you check disk usage of files and folders?
A: du -h --max-depth=1

Q: How do you check which ports are being used?
A: nestat -tuln
